{"id":"6d88f5d0-aca1-43f9-a56a-46c020c83386","object":"chat.completion","created":1785003008,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n        normalized_gain = (loss_without - loss_with) / tokens\\n        normalized_gain = round(normalized_gain, 6)\\n        accepted = parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted,\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain\\n        })\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) for task AGENT-TF-01. The case payload has threshold and calls list. Each call has call_id, loss_without_call, loss_with_call, prediction_tokens, parseable. We need to compute normalized_gain = (loss_without_call - loss_with_call) / prediction_tokens. Then filter: parseable == true and normalized_gain >= threshold. Then accepted_call_ids are those call_ids that satisfy. Diagnostics list for each call in original order, with accepted boolean, call_id, normalized_gain (rounded? probably to some decimal? The schema says number, no rounding specified in schema, but candidate says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\". Need to decide rounding. Usually in such tasks, they round to some precision, maybe default? Could be 6 decimal places? Check fixtures: The